The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```java
if (arena.isRunning()) {
    if (lockFoodLevel) {
        event.setCancelled(true);
    }
}
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the food level lock is applied to all players when the arena is running and the lock is enabled, without checking if the player is actually in the arena. This results in unintended consequences for players outside the arena, as their food level changes are also cancelled.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
if (arena.inArena(p) && lockFoodLevel) {
    event.setCancelled(true);
}
```
Reason:
The fix adds a condition to check if the player is in the arena before applying the food level lock. This ensures that only players within the arena are affected by the food level change event when the lock is enabled, preventing unintended effects on players outside the arena.

